course: dictionary
lesson: 13554
title: Making it up on the spot
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Improvisation means making something up on the spot, without a script or a plan. You do not practise it first; you invent it as you go. «The actors had no script, so they made up the scene as they went along.» That is improvisation.
explain: Improvisation can happen in drama, music and speech. In drama it is often called «improv». Jazz players improvise solos, which means they play a tune they invent in the moment. «The jazz pianist played a wild solo, all improvisation.»
explain: Improvisation can also mean solving a problem with what you have when you lack the proper things. «We had no rope, so we tied our jumpers together.» That is a bit of improvisation. Look at the clues: no rope, so something else is used. Improvisation is a noun.
fact: Improvisation is a noun.
fact: «Improvisation» means making something up on the spot, without a script or plan.
fact: «Improv» is a short, everyday name for drama improvisation.
fact: Improvisation can also mean using whatever you have to fix a problem quickly.
fact: An improvisation can be the piece itself: a tune, scene or speech made up in the moment.
exercise: «The actors had no script, so they made up the scene as they went.» What does improvisation mean here? | Reading the lines from a book | Painting the stage | Practising the same scene for a week | *Making something up on the spot
exercise: «We had no rope, so we tied the jumpers together with our belts.» What kind of improvisation is this? | *Using what you have to solve a problem | Playing music in a band | Writing a letter to a friend | Acting out a story
exercise: «The jazz pianist started an improvisation that nobody had heard before.» Find and copy the word that means a piece made up in the moment. | heard | jazz | *improvisation | pianist
test: Jayden says improv is the same as reading from a script. Why is he wrong? | Improv is only done by singers | Improv means reading very carefully | *Improv is made up on the spot, with no script | Improv needs a script to work
test: «Lost on the hill, Mia made a shelter from a tarp and two sticks.» What does this show? | *Improvisation: using what you have to solve a problem | A plan made a week in advance | Copying someone else's shelter | Nothing to do with problems
exam: «The jazz band played an improvisation, a solo nobody had rehearsed.» Which words show the solo was not planned beforehand? | *nobody had rehearsed | a solo | jazz band | played an
